From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: compact PIN pad reaches the MotionLayout it lives in

On the Q25 the PIN pad showed Android's 166 px round keys over the
message and PIN field (owner report 2026-11-12, uiautomator: key0
[277,385][443,551], flow1 [0,49][720,551]). The compact sizes from 0315
went into the keys' layout params and, only when mContainerMotionLayout
was set, into the scene's constraint sets. That field is set only when
the small-landscape flag is on; with it off, keyguard_pin_motion_layout
is still inflated, and a MotionLayout lays its children out from its
constraint sets, so the layout params were ignored.

applySableCompactPad now takes pin_container itself whenever it is a
MotionLayout, writes the compact key sizes and emergency margins into
every constraint set it has (getConstraintSetIds), updates each state
and asks for a new layout. No authentication code changes.
---
 .../com/android/keyguard/KeyguardPINView.java | 22 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/keyguard/KeyguardPINView.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/keyguard/KeyguardPINView.java
index 2a20b9a..c294b2c 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/keyguard/KeyguardPINView.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/keyguard/KeyguardPINView.java
@@ -258,11 +258,22 @@ public class KeyguardPINView extends KeyguardPinBasedInputView {
                         row0.getPaddingRight(), gap);
             }
         }
-        if (mContainerMotionLayout != null) {
+        // SableOS: the PIN pad is a MotionLayout whenever keyguard_pin_motion_layout is inflated,
+        // even when the small-landscape flag is off and mContainerMotionLayout stays null. A
+        // MotionLayout lays its children out from its scene's constraint sets, not their layout
+        // params, so the compact sizes must go into every set or Android's keys stay.
+        View container = findViewById(R.id.pin_container);
+        MotionLayout motion = container instanceof MotionLayout
+                ? (MotionLayout) container : mContainerMotionLayout;
+        if (motion != null) {
             int ecaMargin = px(pad.ecaMargin, density);
-            for (int id : new int[] {R.id.single_constraints,
-                    R.id.half_folded_single_constraints, R.id.split_constraints}) {
-                ConstraintSet set = mContainerMotionLayout.getConstraintSet(id);
+            int[] ids = motion.getConstraintSetIds();
+            if (ids == null) {
+                ids = new int[] {R.id.single_constraints, R.id.half_folded_single_constraints,
+                        R.id.split_constraints};
+            }
+            for (int id : ids) {
+                ConstraintSet set = motion.getConstraintSet(id);
                 if (set == null) {
                     continue;
                 }
@@ -281,8 +292,9 @@ public class KeyguardPINView extends KeyguardPinBasedInputView {
                 set.setMargin(R.id.keyguard_selector_fade_container, ConstraintSet.TOP, ecaMargin);
                 set.setMargin(R.id.keyguard_selector_fade_container, ConstraintSet.BOTTOM,
                         ecaMargin);
-                mContainerMotionLayout.updateState(id, set);
+                motion.updateState(id, set);
             }
+            motion.requestLayout();
         }
     }
 
